{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790966887,"nonce":"XbVc0CkNoYY22YMVq565wyckf7I=","message":"2026-10-02, lists: the Python frontend passes list[T] by value as a three-word struct, %List{ i64 data, i64 len, i64 cap } (HIR of def history() -\u003e list[float] and def total(xs: list[float])), which the C boundary passes and returns indirectly, so the dispatch's call table cannot make the call. caribou now publishes any struct passed by value as HSTRUCT and refuses it (before, ZynML's Point.origin() was refused only because HOBJ was). The way through is the one tuples take (publish::bridge_tuple_returns): typed-AST wrappers that box a list result into an Any with the frontend's own list boxer, and unbox an Any list parameter, plus a sequence proxy in the core (len/index/set_index/iterate) over the box. That last part needs zyntax_embed::foreign to say how a list box lays its elements out by kind, as it does for tuples.","files":null}]}